            "review_comments": [
                "I would keep `+set modify-date` and `+set create-date` unless we can identify which ImageMagick versions output these and make sure they are not in use anymore:\r\n```suggestion\r\n    has_attached_file :avatar, styles: ->(f) { avatar_styles(f) }, convert_options: { all: '+profile \"!icc,*\" +set modify-date +set create-date +set date:modify +set date:create +set date:timestamp' }, processors: [:lazy_thumbnail]\r\n```",
                "Did some further testing, it seems like the old flags are broken on ImageMagick versions 7.1.1 (latest release), 6.9.10 (used on Ubuntu 20.04), and 6.9.11 (used on current Debian/Ubuntu), but do indeed work with 6.9.12 (latest legacy). The new flags seem to work on all versions listed above, so I don't see the old flags being of much use here."
            ]
